-- ccc29-xxviii-6-part-xxviii.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART XXVIII, "Miscellaneous": sections 841 to 847 (electronic documents), 848 (repealed)
-- and 849 (forms). Layer 1: the law, objectively. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text. The French equivalents after a defined term are quoted and not encoded.
-- The conventions of ccc29-xxviii-0-peace-810.l4 apply unchanged. "An Act or the rules of court" are the sources the text points to; whether a
-- given Act or rule of court allows the dealing is an input (a fact the person states), never decided here.

§ `Section 841 -- Definitions (electronic documents)`

-- 841 The definitions in this section apply in this section and in sections 842 to 847.
-- src:17316 | Definitions
-- src:17317 | 841 The definitions in this section apply in this section and in sections 842 to 847.
@ref Criminal Code s 841 lead-in (src:17316-17317)
GIVEN `the section number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 841 the definitions apply` MEANS
    IF `the section number` AT LEAST 841 AND `the section number` AT MOST 847
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in this section and in sections 842 to 847"

-- data means representations of information or concepts, in any form.
-- src:17318 | data means representations of information or concepts, in any form. (données)
@ref Criminal Code s 841 "data" (src:17318)
GIVEN `it is a representation of information or concepts, in any form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 841 data` MEANS
    IF `it is a representation of information or concepts, in any form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "data means representations of information or concepts, in any form"

-- electronic document means data that is recorded or stored on any medium in or by a computer system or other similar device and that can be read or perceived by a person or a computer system or other similar device. It includes a display, print-out or other output of the data and any document, record, order, exhibit, notice or form that contains the data.
-- src:17319 | electronic document means data that is recorded or stored on any medium in or by a computer system or other similar device and that can be read or perceived by a person or a computer system or other similar device. It includes a display, print-out or other output of the data and any document, record, order, exhibit, notice or form that contains the data. (document électronique)
@ref Criminal Code s 841 "electronic document" (src:17319)
GIVEN `it is data, by s 841 data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is recorded or stored on any medium in or by a computer system or other similar device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it can be read or perceived by a person or a computer system or other similar device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a display, print-out or other output of the data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a document, record, order, exhibit, notice or form that contains the data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 841 electronic document` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is data, by s 841 data` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `it is recorded or stored on any medium in or by a computer system or other similar device` AND `it can be read or perceived by a person or a computer system or other similar device` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is a display, print-out or other output of the data` THEN JUST TRUE   -- "It includes a display, print-out or other output of the data"
        IF `it is a document, record, order, exhibit, notice or form that contains the data` THEN JUST TRUE   -- "and any document, record, order, exhibit, notice or form that contains the data"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "It includes a display, print-out or other output of the data and any document, record, order, exhibit, notice or form that contains the data"

§ `Sections 842 to 847 -- Electronic documents`

-- 842 Despite anything in this Act, a court may create, collect, receive, store, transfer, distribute, publish or otherwise deal with electronic documents if it does so in accordance with an Act or with the rules of court.
-- src:17320 | Dealing with data in court
-- src:17321 | 842 Despite anything in this Act, a court may create, collect, receive, store, transfer, distribute, publish or otherwise deal with electronic documents if it does so in accordance with an Act or with the rules of court.
@ref Criminal Code s 842 (src:17320-17321)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "if it does so in accordance with an Act or with the rules of court" (fork F-842)
GIVEN `it is a court dealing with electronic documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does so in accordance with an Act or with the rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 842 a court may create, collect, receive, store, transfer, distribute, publish or otherwise deal with electronic documents` MEANS
    IF `it is a court dealing with electronic documents` AND `it does so in accordance with an Act or with the rules of court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it does so in accordance with an Act or with the rules of court"

-- 843(1) Despite anything in this Act, a court may accept the transfer of data by electronic means if the transfer is made in accordance with the laws of the place where the transfer originates or the laws of the place where the data is received.
-- src:17322 | Transfer of data
-- src:17323 | 843 (1) Despite anything in this Act, a court may accept the transfer of data by electronic means if the transfer is made in accordance with the laws of the place where the transfer originates or the laws of the place where the data is received.
@ref Criminal Code s 843(1) (src:17322-17323)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gate "if the transfer is made in accordance with the laws of the place where the transfer originates or the laws of the place where the data is received" (fork F-843-1)
GIVEN `it is a court accepting the transfer of data by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is made in accordance with the laws of the place where the transfer originates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is made in accordance with the laws of the place where the data is received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 843(1) a court may accept the transfer of data by electronic means` MEANS
    IF `it is a court accepting the transfer of data by electronic means` AND (`the transfer is made in accordance with the laws of the place where the transfer originates` OR `the transfer is made in accordance with the laws of the place where the data is received`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the transfer is made in accordance with the laws of the place where the transfer originates or the laws of the place where the data is received"

-- 843(2) If a document is required to be filed in a court and the filing is done by transfer of data by electronic means, the filing is complete when the transfer is accepted by the court.
-- src:17324 | Time of filing
-- src:17325 | (2) If a document is required to be filed in a court and the filing is done by transfer of data by electronic means, the filing is complete when the transfer is accepted by the court.
@ref Criminal Code s 843(2) (src:17324-17325)
GIVEN `a document is required to be filed in a court and the filing is done by transfer of data by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is accepted by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 843(2) the filing is complete` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a document is required to be filed in a court and the filing is done by transfer of data by electronic means` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a document is required to be filed in a court and the filing is done by transfer of data by electronic means"
        IF NOT `the transfer is accepted by the court` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the filing is complete when the transfer is accepted by the court"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 844 A requirement under this Act that a document be made in writing is satisfied by the making of the document in electronic form in accordance with an Act or the rules of court.
-- src:17326 | Documents in writing
-- src:17327 | 844 A requirement under this Act that a document be made in writing is satisfied by the making of the document in electronic form in accordance with an Act or the rules of court.
@ref Criminal Code s 844 (src:17326-17327)
GIVEN `the requirement is a requirement under this Act that a document be made in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is made in electronic form in accordance with an Act or the rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 844 the requirement that a document be made in writing is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is a requirement under this Act that a document be made in writing` AND `the document is made in electronic form in accordance with an Act or the rules of court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is satisfied by the making of the document in electronic form in accordance with an Act or the rules of court"

-- 845 If this Act requires a document to be signed, the court may accept a signature in an electronic document if the signature is made in accordance with an Act or the rules of court.
-- src:17328 | Signatures
-- src:17329 | 845 If this Act requires a document to be signed, the court may accept a signature in an electronic document if the signature is made in accordance with an Act or the rules of court.
@ref Criminal Code s 845 (src:17328-17329)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gates "If this Act requires a document to be signed" and "if the signature is made in accordance with an Act or the rules of court" (fork F-845)
GIVEN `this Act requires a document to be signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature is made in accordance with an Act or the rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 845 the court may accept a signature in an electronic document` MEANS
    IF `this Act requires a document to be signed` AND `the signature is made in accordance with an Act or the rules of court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the signature is made in accordance with an Act or the rules of court"

-- 846 If under this Act an information, an affidavit or a solemn declaration or a statement under oath or solemn affirmation is to be made by a person, the court may accept it in the form of an electronic document if (a) the person states in the electronic document that all matters contained in the information, affidavit, solemn declaration or statement are true to his or her knowledge and belief; (b) the person before whom it is made or sworn is authorized to take or receive informations, affidavits, solemn declarations or statements and he or she states in the electronic document that the information, affidavit, solemn declaration or statement was made under oath, solemn declaration or solemn affirmation, as the case may be; and (c) the electronic document was made in accordance with the laws of the place where it was made.
-- src:17330 | Oaths
-- src:17331 | 846 If under this Act an information, an affidavit or a solemn declaration or a statement under oath or solemn affirmation is to be made by a person, the court may accept it in the form of an electronic document if
-- src:17332 | (a) the person states in the electronic document that all matters contained in the information, affidavit, solemn declaration or statement are true to his or her knowledge and belief;
-- src:17333 | (b) the person before whom it is made or sworn is authorized to take or receive informations, affidavits, solemn declarations or statements and he or she states in the electronic document that the information, affidavit, solemn declaration or statement was made under oath, solemn declaration or solemn affirmation, as the case may be; and
-- src:17334 | (c) the electronic document was made in accordance with the laws of the place where it was made.
@ref Criminal Code s 846 to s 846(c) (src:17330-17334)
-- @name-test: flipped to NOTHING; gates "If under this Act an information ... is to be made" and "if (a), (b) and (c)" (fork F-846)
GIVEN `under this Act an information, an affidavit, a solemn declaration or a statement under oath or solemn affirmation is to be made by a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person states in the electronic document that all matters contained in it are true to his or her knowledge and belief` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person before whom it is made or sworn is authorized to take or receive it and states in the electronic document that it was made under oath, solemn declaration or solemn affirmation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic document was made in accordance with the laws of the place where it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 846 the court may accept the information, affidavit, solemn declaration or statement in the form of an electronic document` MEANS
    IF `under this Act an information, an affidavit, a solemn declaration or a statement under oath or solemn affirmation is to be made by a person`
       AND `the person states in the electronic document that all matters contained in it are true to his or her knowledge and belief`
       AND `the person before whom it is made or sworn is authorized to take or receive it and states in the electronic document that it was made under oath, solemn declaration or solemn affirmation`
       AND `the electronic document was made in accordance with the laws of the place where it was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..."

-- 847 Any person who is entitled to obtain a copy of a document from a court is entitled, in the case of a document in electronic form, to obtain a printed copy of the electronic document from the court on payment of a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the relevant province.
-- src:17335 | Copies
-- src:17336 | 847 Any person who is entitled to obtain a copy of a document from a court is entitled, in the case of a document in electronic form, to obtain a printed copy of the electronic document from the court on payment of a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the relevant province.
@ref Criminal Code s 847 (src:17335-17336)
-- @name-test: listed, "entitled" (F-847): "in the case of a document in electronic form" answers NOTHING; "on payment of a reasonable fee" answers JUST FALSE
GIVEN `the person is entitled to obtain a copy of a document from a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person pays a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the relevant province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 847 the person is entitled to obtain a printed copy of the electronic document from the court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is entitled to obtain a copy of a document from a court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who is entitled to obtain a copy of a document from a court"
        IF NOT `the document is in electronic form` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a document in electronic form"
        IF NOT `the person pays a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees fixed or approved by the Attorney General of the relevant province` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on payment of a reasonable fee determined in accordance with a tariff of fees"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 849 -- Forms`

-- 849(1) The forms set out in this Part, varied to suit the case, or forms to the like effect are deemed to be good, valid and sufficient in the circumstances for which they are provided.
-- src:17341 | 849 (1) The forms set out in this Part, varied to suit the case, or forms to the like effect are deemed to be good, valid and sufficient in the circumstances for which they are provided.
@ref Criminal Code s 849(1) (src:17341)
GIVEN `it is a form set out in this Part, varied to suit the case, or a form to the like effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used in the circumstances for which it is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 849(1) the form is deemed to be good, valid and sufficient` MEANS
    IF `it is a form set out in this Part, varied to suit the case, or a form to the like effect` AND `it is used in the circumstances for which it is provided`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the circumstances for which they are provided"

-- 849(2) No justice is required to attach or affix a seal to any writing or process that he or she is authorized to issue and in respect of which a form is provided by this Part.
-- src:17342 | Seal not required
-- src:17343 | (2) No justice is required to attach or affix a seal to any writing or process that he or she is authorized to issue and in respect of which a form is provided by this Part.
@ref Criminal Code s 849(2) (src:17342-17343)
GIVEN `it is a writing or process that the justice is authorized to issue and in respect of which a form is provided by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 849(2) the justice is required to attach or affix a seal` MEANS
    IF `it is a writing or process that the justice is authorized to issue and in respect of which a form is provided by this Part`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No justice is required to attach or affix a seal"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any writing or process that he or she is authorized to issue and in respect of which a form is provided by this Part"

-- 849(3) Any pre-printed portions of a form set out in this Part, varied to suit the case, or of a form to the like effect shall be printed in both official languages.
-- src:17344 | Official languages
-- src:17345 | (3) Any pre-printed portions of a form set out in this Part, varied to suit the case, or of a form to the like effect shall be printed in both official languages.
@ref Criminal Code s 849(3) (src:17344-17345)
GIVEN `it is a pre-printed portion of a form set out in this Part, varied to suit the case, or of a form to the like effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 849(3) the pre-printed portion is required to be printed in both official languages` MEANS
    IF `it is a pre-printed portion of a form set out in this Part, varied to suit the case, or of a form to the like effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any pre-printed portions of a form set out in this Part"
